pires-forge (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release of Pires Forge 1.0.0.
  * Rebrand: Rayforge -> Pires Forge (display name, AppStream ID,
    .desktop, .metainfo, Debian package, Python binary entry point).
    The Python module path 'rayforge/' and addon names
    'rayforge-addon-*' are KEPT identical to upstream for
    addon-compat and Python module compat.
  * All GitHub URLs (GITHUB_RELEASES_API, GITHUB_URL, ISSUES_URL,
    DOWNLOAD_URL) now point to yuri-schmaltz/pires-forge (this fork).
  * Application update check defaults to off (was: on, pointing to
    upstream). Users can opt-in via Settings -> Preferences.
  * Add python3-defusedxml to Depends: (required by
    rayforge.image.lightburn.importer since PR #14; blocks
    billion-laughs, XXE, and DTD-SSRF attacks).
  * i18n fix: .mo translation files are now bundled in the .deb
    (MANIFEST.in updated to include .po/.pot, plus a compile
    step in CI). Closes the silent "I selected Portuguese but
    the UI is still in English" bug.
  * Maintainer: Yuri Schmaltz <security@yuri-schmaltz.dev>.
  * 33 regression tests in tests/shared/util/test_i18n_shipped.py
    verify every supported language ships in the binary.

 -- Yuri Schmaltz <security@yuri-schmaltz.dev>  Sun, 03 Aug 2026 09:30:00 +0000

pires-forge (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Update maintainer to Yuri Schmaltz <security@yuri-schmaltz.dev>
    (fork maintained at github.com/yuri-schmaltz/rayforge).
  * Add python3-defusedxml to Depends: (required by
    rayforge.image.lightburn.importer since PR #14, was
    failing at import time on user installations).
  * Rebrand: Rayforge -> Pires Forge (display name, AppStream ID,
    Debian package, Python binary entry point). The Python module path
    'rayforge/' and addon names 'rayforge-addon-*' are KEPT for
    upstream and addon-compat.

 -- Yuri Schmaltz <security@yuri-schmaltz.dev>  Sat, 01 Aug 2026 01:07:32 +0000
